<!--Post: 750--><!--Time: 1092494379-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST750"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, August 14, 2004 - 7:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->May 11, 1997: Deanna Law, 53, was found strangled in her home at 1423 S. Market. She was sexually assaulted, and her nude body was found in the bathtub. A neighbor was charged with second-degree murder, but the charge was dropped after his lawyer contended that he faked the confession. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 750-->
<!--Post: 762--><!--Time: 1092538659-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST762"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, August 14, 2004 - 7:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.wichitasedgwickcountycrimestoppers.com/unsolved_murders/law.html" target=_top>http://www.wichitasedgwickcountycrimestoppers.com/ unsolved_murders/law.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 762-->
<!--Post: 764--><!--Time: 1092548749-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST764"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, August 14, 2004 - 10:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Flytodeb, <BR>Wow! Thank you. It&#39;s still an unsolved case. The article does point at less than excellent police work. Yet again...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 764-->
<!--Post: 820--><!--Time: 1092932375-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST820"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, August 19, 2004 - 9:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The MO used on Deanna matches the signature of John Brewer, who is serving a life term in New Hampshire. He killed one woman there and one in Florida. He raped, strangled, and placed the bodies in the bathtub. He was still at large at the time of Deanna&#39;s death.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 820-->
<!--Post: 821--><!--Time: 1092941484-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST821"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rachel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rachel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, August 19, 2004 - 11:51 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Teardrop~ <BR> <BR>Do you know if LE has any DNA samples from Law&#39;s crime scene and, if so, have they tested for comparison to Brewer? Thank you. <BR> <BR>Rachel<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 821-->
<!--Post: 822--><!--Time: 1092942742-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST822"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, August 19, 2004 - 12:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There is DNA on Brewer. That is how they got a conviction on him. The Law case I do not know. I did notify Crimestoppers about John Brewer the other day. They will have to run matches if they have any from Deanna. That may take some time for the wheels to turn.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 822-->
<!--Post: 823--><!--Time: 1092945010-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST823"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, August 19, 2004 - 12:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Teardrop, the wheels may turn slowly, but slow means sure. A 1984 cold case murder in Kansas City, not BTK related, was solved by DNA and just announced two days ago. I am very hopeful that DNA from the 1986 Wegerle murder may yield results. If the DNA does not match a suspect in the data base, at least it might match some of the cold cases in Wichita, and when they do find the culprit, several cases will be solved at the same time. <BR>-Deb <BR><a href="http://www.wdaftv4.com/fullstory.asp?ID=5204" target=_top>http://www.wdaftv4.com/fullstory.asp?ID=5204</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 823-->
<!--Post: 828--><!--Time: 1093016920-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST828"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, August 20, 2004 - 8:48 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Flytodeb:  All things come to those who wait?! Thanks for the link. <BR> <BR>Only a fool would leave DNA at the crime scene. <BR> <BR>With BTK&#39;s cunning and his background in who knows what, he might be aware that he may be the one in however many, whose semen and blood type do not match. That was the case with the Red Ripper, who was eventually caught because the Russians require people to check in and out of everywhere they go.  Tedious and time consuming, but it paid off for them. <BR> <BR>And, thanks to the Warren Supreme Court, who gave criminals more rights than the victims/public, some police work does appear inept. Cops have to watch so many rules that much of their concentration is on that aspect first, and collection of evidence, second.  Blinders and prejudice also play a huge part as well. There was a triple murder in Houston. It was ruled a murder-suicide because the wife/mother of the family was not wearing underwear. All the evidence was screaming to the contrary. The cop who would not quit finally brought the hitman to justice.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 828-->
